      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <h3>What is project management for AI agents?</h3>
      <p>It's the practice of planning, assigning, and verifying work done by AI agents — with issue tracking that captures evidence of what an agent actually changed, usage KPIs for tokens and time, and machine-readable access so agents can read and update the board themselves.</p>
      <h3>Can agents work in normal tools like Jira or Trello?</h3>
      <p>Partially, through API integrations. But generic trackers don't model claims vs. evidence, don't track per-agent token and cost KPIs, and don't enforce human-only merges. Teams end up compensating with comments and manual checks, which stops scaling as agent volume grows.</p>
      <h3>How do I keep AI agents from shipping broken code?</h3>
      <p>Require every agent task to end at a review state with the diff and proof attached to the issue, keep the merge as a human action, and scope autonomy explicitly — let an agent leave a branch or open a PR, but only grant merge rights after checks pass and only if you say so.</p>
